  {
    "id": "g-imperative-polite",
    "title": "fale, falem",
    "summary": "polite commands, and to more than one person",
    "intro": [
      "To be polite (o senhor, a senhora, você), use the swapped vowel without the -s: fale, coma, abra. It's the same with or without não: Fale mais devagar. Não fale tão alto.",
      "To more than one person (vocês), add -m: falem, comam, abram.",
      "These are the forms you'll see on signs and hear in directions: Vire à direita. Siga em frente."
    ],
    "tables": [
      { "verb": "polite commands", "caption": "Polite · to more than one person", "listen": "form", "rows": [
        { "person": "falar", "form": "fale · falem" },
        { "person": "comer", "form": "coma · comam" },
        { "person": "abrir", "form": "abra · abram" },
        { "person": "fazer", "form": "faça · façam" },
        { "person": "dizer", "form": "diga · digam" },
        { "person": "ir", "form": "vá · vão" },
        { "person": "vir", "form": "venha · venham" },
        { "person": "ter", "form": "tenha · tenham" },
        { "person": "ser", "form": "seja · sejam" },
        { "person": "dar", "form": "dê · deem" }
      ] }
    ],
    "examples": [
      { "pt": "Vire à direita e siga em frente.", "en": "Turn right and go straight on." },
      { "pt": "Diga!", "en": "Yes? Go ahead! (staff at a counter)" },
      { "pt": "Tenha um bom dia!", "en": "Have a good day!" },
      { "pt": "Venham jantar connosco!", "en": "Come and have dinner with us! (to several people)" }
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Diga? at a counter or on the phone means \"Yes? Go ahead.\"",
      "Esteja à vontade = Make yourself at home.",
      "Deem (give, plural) used to be written dêem."
    ],
